.po 1i
.TH LOGNAME 3 Bell
.V 08/15/84 17:21:32
.\"@[$]logname.3	1.5 08/15/84 17:21:32 - Zilog Inc
.SH NAME
logname \- login name of user
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "char \(**logname(\|);"\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Logname\^
returns a pointer to the null-terminated login name;
it extracts the \fB\s-1$LOGNAME\s+1\fP 
variable from the user's environment.
.PP
This routine is kept in
.BR /usr/lib/lib\s-1PW\s+1.a .
.SH FILES
/etc/profile
.SH SEE ALSO
env(1),
login(1),
profile(5),
environ(7).
